# Textus Knowledge Lake CML Model

> NOTE FOR CODEX
>
> This file is the canonical CML source location for the TKL application model.
> Replace this scaffold with valid current CML syntax after checking the CML/Cozy implementation and existing examples.
> Do not invent unsupported CML syntax.
>
> Design source:
> - docs/notes/application-model.md
> - docs/notes/architecture.md
> - docs/journal/2026-09-23-tkl-core-architecture-consolidation.md
>
> Modeling intent:
> - Model application-level Use Cases separately from execution Workflows.
> - Keep future TKL Use Cases in the application model even when they are outside Phase 1.
> - Phase 1 primary Use Case is "Propose Knowledge Candidate".
> - The Phase 1 Application Workflow realizes that Use Case end-to-end through KnowledgeHub Admission.
> - Derive/associate Application Capabilities where supported by current CML.
> - Use current CML concepts for Use Case Slice / executable specification only if they are actually supported.
>
> Primary application areas:
> 1. Knowledge Acquisition
>    - Propose Knowledge Candidate [Phase 1 primary]
>    - Explore Candidates by Theme
>    - Discover Candidates from New Evidence
>    - Inspect Candidate Evidence
>    - Compare Candidate with Existing Knowledge
>    - Revise Candidate
>    - Submit Candidate for Admission
>    - Hold or Reject Candidate
> 2. Research / Exploration
> 3. Project Awareness
> 4. Content Production
>
> Phase 1 workflow outline:
> Determine Knowledgeization Scope
> -> Resolve Knowledge Resources
> -> Collect Evidence
> -> Normalize Evidence
> -> Prepare Knowledge Material
> -> Persist PreparedMaterial
> -> Extract Knowledge Candidate
> -> Compare Existing Knowledge
> -> Compose Candidate Proposal
> -> Human Review
> -> Submit to KnowledgeHub Admission
>
> Important domain concepts to align with the model:
> - KnowledgeResource / provider-independent resource identity
> - Evidence
> - Communication Value Objects
> - PreparedMaterial Entity
> - KnowledgeCandidate
> - Provenance / Lineage
> - Admission boundary
>
> Provider-specific Google Workspace / Slack details are implementation mappings,
> not the semantic core of this CML model.
>
